TIP:  The opening chords for the intro are single strums with a pause in between each one.  (F7) and (F3) are really just (B) and (G) played as an F-shape at different frets.  There should be position markers on your fretboard to make them easy to find.  And you need that 4th string on the (D/A4) - which is just (D) with your pinky added to the 4th string/4th fret - and there will be time coming off the last (F7) to get squared away. 
         

